{
  "method_version": "1.0.0",
  "_method_version": "1.0.0 promotes three figures and a verifier from a larger workspace recipe, chosen because each isolates one counting artefact that generalises past this register. Two of the three replace a published wrong version, both kept in the write-up rather than deleted: a firm-count-against-national-share scatter that measured average firm size and ranked the most equal route as the most concentrated, and a log-log path chart whose eleven wandering lines asserted routes the categories may not have taken. The Gini trend exists only because the flat all-firms series was checked against a fixed-count one.",
